    "shift": "shift_1"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The position-time graphs for two students <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> returning from the school to their homes are shown in figure.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0041_c8430e3fe3d6.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 236px;\" /></p><p>(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> lives closer to the school</p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> lives closer to the school</p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> takes lesser time to reach home</p><p>(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> travels faster than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>(E) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> travels faster than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfenced></math> only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfenced></math> only",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfenced></math> only",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>From the position time graph the velocity is found out by the slope of the line. The slope is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>The slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. Hence, the velocity of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is greater than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. As can be seen from the graph&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>. So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;lives closer to the school and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math>. Hence, this is the correct option.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}